            <ArticleTitle>[Microsurgery of common discal sciatica. Technics and results].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>371-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors report their own experience of microsurgery for surgical treatment of lumbar disc herniation. Series include 30 cases with a one year of mean follow up. Comparative studies are discussed according to others microsurgical series already published. Good care of peridural fat and gently retraction of the root seem to be main factors for good functional result.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
